Maintainer: Sebastian Matkovich <sebastian.matkovich@gmail.com>
Build-Depends: debhelper-compat (= 13), qtbase5-dev, qtdeclarative5-dev,
 libalarm-dev, libdbus-1-dev, libtime-dev, pkg-config
Standards-Version: 4.6.2
Homepage: https://github.com/smatkovi/meego-clock
Rules-Requires-Root: no

Package: meego-clock
Architecture: any
Depends: ${shlibs:Depends}, ${misc:Depends}, qt-components,
 qml-module-qtquick2, alarmd, clockd
Description: The Nokia N9's clock for Hildon
 The analog clock with the home city and the alarms, and the alarm editor
 with the N9's two-circle time picker, written anew in QML with the MeeGo
 Harmattan Qt Quick components (com.nokia.meego 2.0, the Qt 5 port of
 qt-components) on Maemo's alarm daemon. Its alarms are the same as Maemo's
 clock's (clock-ui) and ring with the system UI's alarm dialog.
 .
 The N9's theme and fonts are Nokia's and not included: without them the
 components draw with the open base theme.
XB-Maemo-Display-Name: Clock (MeeGo)
